' 10 The theory seam: the gate of a factory call, the admission of a send,
' and the check at a match.
'
' Source of the figure of theory-seam.md (section 3) and of
' f1r3lang-integration.md. The figure restates rules TH-1 to TH-9 of
' specification.md section 5 and the code of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/theory/, spaces/factory/constructor.rs
' (theory_gate) and spaces/generic.rs (Admission::of, Cx::admits,
' check_leases). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. A factory call with free Th(args): gate 4 keeps the identity of a
'      builtin without arguments as bytes in the config (TH-2a, TH-4).
'   2. A send: each config read resolves the identity (TH-3, TH-7), and the
'      checker admits each value in order, before any staging (TH-5).
'   3. A receive: after the where guard, the checker checks each stored
'      datum of the match. A refusal is a guard refusal (TH-6).
'   4. The commit refuses two or more leases (TH-9).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 10-theory-admission.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 10-theory-admission
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The theory seam (P7 step 4): a factory gate, an admission at a send, a check at a match

start
if (the operation?) then (factory call)
  :free Th(args) in the constructor (gate 4, TH-4); <<$rrs_factory>>
  if (Th is Nat, Int, String, Bool or Any?) then (yes)
    if (args?) then (none)
      :config slot "theory" ← one GByteArray
      with the bytes of the builtin identity of Th
      (TH-2, TH-2a, decision 74); <<$rrs_storage>>
      stop
    else (some)
      :BadConstructorArgument; <<$rrs_reject>>
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :UnknownTheory, with the nearest builtin
    within two edits; <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  endif
elseif (send) then
  :read C(sid): decode the identity bytes
  and resolve them (TH-3, TH-7); <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (a checker of this build?) then (no)
    :TheoryUnavailable; <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :admit each value v_i in order, at no charge,
  before any staging or counter bump (TH-5, TH-8); <<$rrs_checker>>
  note right
    TH-1: a builtin decides by shape,
    <latex>\mathrm{sole}(v) \wedge \mathrm{kind}(v) \in \mathrm{Th}</latex>
  end note
  if (the first verdict that is not Proven?) then (Refuted at i)
    :TheoryRefuted(theory, i); <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  elseif (Undetermined at i) then
    :TheoryUndetermined(theory, i); <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  else (none)
    :<color:white>store the datum, or fire a waiter with the datum in flight:</color>
    <color:white>the checker checks no datum in flight (TH-6)</color>; <<$rrs_effect>>
  endif
else (receive)
  :read C(sid): decode the identity bytes
  and resolve them (TH-3, TH-7); <<$rrs_agent>>
  :the first candidate that matches spatially:
  a head, a scan record, a lane head or a join search; <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (the where guard admits the match?) then (yes)
    :check_match on each stored datum of the match,
    with the values that its bind captures (TH-6); <<$rrs_checker>>
    if (every verdict is Proven?) then (yes)
      :<color:white>fire</color>; <<$rrs_effect>>
    else (no)
      :a guard refusal: a scan receive parks, a head blocks,
      a join keeps its search (decision 37); <<$rrs_storage>>
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :a guard refusal; <<$rrs_storage>>
    stop
  endif
endif
if (two or more leases in the transaction (TH-9)?) then (yes)
  :NestedCommitGuard before the commit; <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
  :<color:white>commit</color>; <<$rrs_effect>>
endif
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_factory>  | the factory call |
|<$rrs_agent>    | a step of the plan of the space agent |
|<$rrs_checker>  | the checker of the theory |
|<$rrs_storage>  | the config record, or a parked waiter |
|<$rrs_effect>   | a staged or committed effect |
|<$rrs_reject>   | a failure that aborts the deploy |
endlegend
@enduml
